# The Create React App scaffold pins date-fns 4 beside react-day-picker 8, which peers on
# date-fns 2/3, so this tree only resolves with legacy peer resolution. CI passed
# --legacy-peer-deps on the command line, but Dependabot does not read the workflow: it ran
# its own install, failed to resolve, and so could neither regenerate the lockfile nor open
# a pull request. That is why the postcss bump arrived with package.json updated and the
# lockfile untouched (npm ci then failed EUSAGE, "lock file's postcss@8.5.10 does not
# satisfy postcss@8.5.23"), and why the js-yaml and svgo security updates failed outright.
# Declaring it here puts CI, Dependabot and a human `npm install` on the same resolution.
legacy-peer-deps=true
